WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:11.755
A whole week went by.

2
00:00:11.756 --> 00:00:15.742
Vinnie and Mandy could not go to the attic.

3
00:00:15.743 --> 00:00:20.582
Mom and Dad kept them busy all the time.

4
00:00:20.583 --> 00:00:25.491
On Saturday morning, Vinnie and Mandy got their chance.

5
00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:29.044
Vinnie woke his sister up.

6
00:00:29.045 --> 00:00:32.232
It was still dark.

7
00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:35.407
“What time is it?”

8
00:00:35.408 --> 00:00:38.476
Mandy asked, rubbing her eyes.

9
00:00:38.477 --> 00:00:40.227
“It doesn’t matter.

10
00:00:40.228 --> 00:00:43.150
Come on,” Vinnie whispered.

11
00:00:43.151 --> 00:00:46.743
The children crept up the stairs.

12
00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:50.070
Mandy opened the photo album.

13
00:00:50.071 --> 00:00:54.212
“Look at the Aztec photo,” she said.

14
00:00:54.213 --> 00:00:56.093
Vinnie looked.

15
00:00:56.094 --> 00:00:59.602
“Yeah, that’s us!” he said.

16
00:00:59.603 --> 00:01:04.155
He shivered as he remembered their Aztec travels.

17
00:01:04.156 --> 00:01:09.957
“Where will we go next?” he wondered aloud.

18
00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:13.294
Mandy turned the page.

19
00:01:13.295 --> 00:01:19.579
This time the old man stood in front of a very long ship.

20
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.851
The ship had a huge sail.

21
00:01:22.852 --> 00:01:25.244
It glowed brightly.

22
00:01:25.245 --> 00:01:31.034
Along the side of the ship were 16 large round plates.

23
00:01:31.035 --> 00:01:35.766
They were glowing too.

24
00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:40.502
“What is this?” Vinnie pulled the picture out.

25
00:01:40.503 --> 00:01:43.486
He stared at the glowing photo.

26
00:01:43.487 --> 00:01:47.245
“It looks like . . .” Mandy began.

27
00:01:47.246 --> 00:01:52.935
She couldn’t finish her sentence.

28
00:01:52.936 --> 00:01:58.148
The children fell into the dark tunnel.

29
00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:03.815
“Ow!” grunted Vinnie as he landed on a wooden floor.

30
00:02:03.816 --> 00:02:08.259
“Ugh!” groaned Mandy. “That hurt.

31
00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:10.555
Where are we?”

32
00:02:10.556 --> 00:02:14.217
The children sat up and looked around.

33
00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:18.757
They were surrounded by wooden chests.

34
00:02:18.758 --> 00:02:22.734
A chilly breeze brushed their faces.

35
00:02:22.735 --> 00:02:25.909
They were rocking gently.

36
00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:30.812
“I think we’re on a ship,” whispered Vinnie.

37
00:02:30.813 --> 00:02:34.450
The ship suddenly moved up and down.

38
00:02:34.451 --> 00:02:36.820
Vinnie lost his balance.

39
00:02:36.821 --> 00:02:39.404
“Whoa!” he cried.

40
00:02:39.405 --> 00:02:45.148
He fell backward, flinging his arms wildly.

41
00:02:45.149 --> 00:02:49.506
“Ouch! You hit me,” said a voice.

42
00:02:49.507 --> 00:02:54.572
A boy slowly sat up, rubbing his arm.

43
00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:58.541
Startled, the children stared at him.

44
00:02:58.542 --> 00:03:02.412
The boy’s fair hair and skin were dirty.

45
00:03:02.413 --> 00:03:09.233
He wore a pair of dark pants, fur boots, and a wool cloak.

46
00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:13.414
“Where did you come from?” the boy asked.

47
00:03:13.415 --> 00:03:17.746
“We . . . " Vinnie struggled to answer.

48
00:03:17.747 --> 00:03:20.948
Mandy got up and looked around.

49
00:03:20.949 --> 00:03:24.760
They were on a large open boat.

50
00:03:24.761 --> 00:03:30.475
There were many wooden benches along both sides of the ship.

51
00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:35.761
About ten men were rowing gently with big oars.

52
00:03:35.762 --> 00:03:40.908
Other men were sleeping on the benches, snoring loudly.

53
00:03:40.909 --> 00:03:46.618
One very large man was snoring louder than all of them.

54
00:03:46.619 --> 00:03:49.499
“Hey—you’re a girl!”

55
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:53.872
the boy suddenly said, staring at Mandy.

56
00:03:53.873 --> 00:03:57.895
“So what?” Mandy replied loudly.

57
00:03:57.896 --> 00:04:02.082
“Shh, be quiet,” said the boy.

58
00:04:02.083 --> 00:04:04.936
“You’ll wake him up.”

59
00:04:04.937 --> 00:04:09.072
“Who?” asked Mandy, turning quickly.

60
00:04:09.073 --> 00:04:13.471
As she turned, she knocked over a bag.

61
00:04:13.472 --> 00:04:17.958
It was on top of a barrel and full of iron nails.

62
00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:23.631
The nails scattered loudly all over the wooden deck.

63
00:04:23.632 --> 00:04:29.233
“Him?” Vinnie asked, pointing to the large man.

64
00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:31.426
“Uh-oh, too late.

65
00:04:31.427 --> 00:04:33.875
He’s already awake.”

66
00:04:33.876 --> 00:04:38.942
The man stood up and pulled out a long sword.

67
00:04:38.943 --> 00:04:48.913
“Who dares to board the Sleeping Dragon?” he growled.
